@alangpierce Adding additional locking information to the fix will help in some cases (like the one we are talking about here), but it will cause some valid, non-conflicting autofixes to be skipped. In your example, if we lock the whole range between preceding and following statements `linebreak-style` rule will not be able to modify windows line ending to unix format, since line break operator will be between two statements. In general, there's a good chance that you will prevent whitespace rules to modify the code with this approach.
I guess maybe it's better to not fix some issues, but guarantee correct output? I'm not 100% sure.

P.S. I'm most definitely don't want to discourage you from brainstorming solutions. Just pointing out issues that might come up from this approach.
